          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is induction cooking safe with a pacemaker?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most induction cooktop manuals advise people with pacemakers or implanted defibrillators to keep a sensible distance from active cooking zones and to consult their doctor. Modern implants are well shielded and the magnetic field weakens quickly with distance, but the right answer depends on your specific device, so ask your cardiologist or the device manufacturer before switching."
          }
        }
      ],
    },
