        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Induction is the better cooktop for most people: faster, more efficient, easier to control at low heat, safer around children, cleaner to live with and free of combustion pollutants. Those advantages are real every single day you cook, which is why most people who switch do not go back.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Gas earns its place where the flame itself is the point, where the wiring makes induction a major project, or where the power goes out often and there is no backup. Check your panel and your pans first, ignore the running-cost arguments, and then choose the cooktop that fits how you actually cook.
          </p>
        </div>

